@@ -9362,3 +9362,35 @@ RADM_83=Colour vision
 RADM_84=Colour-blind mode
 RADM_85=Replaces red, green, teal and amber across the interface with colours that stay distinct for colour-blind vision. Only colours change; it applies on every device signed in to this router.
 RADM_86=Standard colours
+RLOG_108=Rx / Tx retries
+RLOG_109=Rx / Tx retries: of the frames the router received from the device / sent to it since it joined, the share that needed a retransmission. A few percent is normal; a high or rising share means a weak or crowded link.
+RNET2_1=The saved look of this sign-in page could not be read. It is kept as it is unless you change the brand name, background or terms.
+RNET2_2=Secured
+RNET2_3=Open
+RNET2_4=Saved at once; the Wi-Fi restarts once, when you press Apply now.
+RDIC_1=Camera
+RDIC_2=Home cinema
+RDIC_3=Wireless headphones
+RDIC_4=Game console
+RDIC_5=Set-top box
+RDIC_6=Device picture
+RDIC_7=Automatic (as detected)
+RDIC_8=Upload a picture
+RDIC_9=Remove the picture
+RDIC_10=PNG, JPEG or WebP. The router keeps a 64 x 64 copy; without a picture the device type icon shows.
+RDIC_11=Device type
+RDIC_12=Picture and device type
+RDIC_13=Only PNG, JPEG or WebP pictures are accepted.
+RDIC_14=The picture is too large.
+RDIC_15=The router already holds 256 device pictures. Remove one first.
+RDIC_16=Not enough free space in the router storage (/jffs).
+RDIC_17=The picture could not be saved on the router.
+RDIC_18=Unknown device type.
+RAPP_1=ASUS Router app
+RAPP_2=The ASUS Router phone app is not tested or supported by Reaper. Reaper checks its requests like a browser's, and the app does not pass those checks. This switch lets the app through on the home network only.
+RAPP_3=Allow the app (home network only)
+RAPP_4=A request that says it comes from the app then skips the cross-site checks: the Referer check, the page token on a save, and the rule that a save must be a POST.
+RAPP_5=Any device or program on the home network can claim to be the app. Everyone still has to sign in with the router's name and password.
+RAPP_6=It never applies to requests from the internet, from guest or other separate networks, or from VPN clients.
+RAPP_7=Parts of the app may still not work: Reaper has removed functions the app expects. Leave this off unless you depend on the app.
+RAPP_8=Allow the ASUS Router app on the home network? Any device there can claim to be the app and skip the cross-site checks. Sign-in is still required. The app is not supported by Reaper.
